# Sample requests (VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains HTTP client).
@base = http://localhost:7071/api

### 1. Function chaining
POST {{base}}/orchestrators/FunctionChainingOrchestrator?wait=10
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "A-100", "customerEmail": "jane@example.com",
  "items": [{ "sku": "BOOK-1", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 15 }, { "sku": "PEN-9", "quantity": 5, "unitPrice": 2 }] }

### 2. Fan-out / fan-in
POST {{base}}/orchestrators/FanOutFanInOrchestrator
Content-Type: application/json

{ "folder": "invoices/2026-10", "fileCount": 10 }

### 3a. Async HTTP API: start (returns 202 + Location)
POST {{base}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reportName": "Q3-sales", "sections": 5 }

### 3b. Async HTTP API: poll (paste the instanceId from 3a)
GET {{base}}/reports/<instanceId>/status

### 4. Monitor
POST {{base}}/orchestrators/MonitorOrchestrator
Content-Type: application/json

{ "jobId": "job-42", "pollingIntervalSeconds": 10, "expiryMinutes": 5 }

### 5a. Human interaction: start (approve/reject links are printed in the func host log)
POST {{base}}/approvals
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestedBy": "jane", "description": "New laptop", "amount": 2400,
  "approverEmail": "manager@example.com", "timeoutMinutes": 2 }

### 5b. Human interaction: respond (copy the link from the log)
GET {{base}}/approvals/<instanceId>/respond?decision=approve&token=<token>
